// Dll/Player/PlayerSlots.inc - the player interface vtable, one line per slot
// in slot order (the order GCC assigned them, so declaration order matters).
//
//   PLAYER_SLOT(offset, return type, name, (params), base)
//
// base: 1 = PlayerBase implements it (address in PlayerBase.cpp), 0 = pure in
// PlayerBase too, every player module provides it. Slots +0x000..+0x008 (the
// destructors and DllObject::release) are declared by the classes themselves.
// Names are inferred unless a comment says otherwise. Parameter lists come
// from register use (argument 1 = this, ints in argument 2.., floats in float argument 1.. taking an integer slot
// each); see decomp analysis player_vtable_dllsoma.json for the addresses.
// IPlayer ends at +0x46C; +0x470..+0x480 (PLAYER_SLOT_BASE)
// are new in PlayerBase.

